  "body": "Why is it usefull to have a menu element with type context inside a menu list, when the same functionality is doable with another combination\r\n\r\nExample why is this better (semantic, backward compatibilty, logic, html syntax principle):\r\n\r\n```\r\n<menu> \r\n <li>\r\n  <button type=menu value=\"Help\" menu=\"helpmenu\">\r\n  <menu id=\"helpmenu\" type=\"context\">\r\n   <menuitem onclick=\"location='help.html'\" label=\"Help\">\r\n   <menuitem onclick=\"location='about.html'\" label=\"About\">\r\n  </menu>\r\n </li>\r\n</menu>\r\n```\r\n\r\nThan something like this\r\n\r\n```\r\n<ul role=\"menu>\r\n<li>\r\n<details id=\"helpmenu\" role=\"drop-down-menu\">\r\n  <summary>Help</summary>\r\n\r\n  <a href=\"/help.html\">Help</a>\r\n  <a href=\"/about.html\">About</a>\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n```\r\n\r\nMaybe for slightly less CSS rules , converge with android xml style or why should this menu type context exist ? Thanks.\r\n\r\nExample taken from https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/forms.html#the-menu-element\r\nPreview of first example https://html.spec.whatwg.org/images/sample-toolbar-1.png\r\nEdit: Question clarification, updated example",
